{# One job: a lean, buildable v1 spec. Coding agents implement it next, so every
   feature needs acceptance checks runnable without a printer. #}
{{ config(output_format="json") }}
Write the v1 build spec for this project. The README's scope table is binding:
anything marked Exclude or Defer must appear only under "out_of_scope". Where the
research contradicts a README decision, keep the decision and record the
conflict under "open_questions" (do not silently change it).

Lessons from earlier drafts (follow them):
- Under 32 mm is NOT a fail: the end block switches to a nozzle push
  (`{if max_layer_z > 41} ... {else} G1 Z1`). Height may only warn, never fail.
- Lean v1: at most 3 synchronous API endpoints, no job queue, no polling, no
  acknowledgement flow. At most 4 acceptance checks per feature.
- Features are things the running app does. The research node is a build-time
  input, not a feature.
- Be terse: one sentence per field.

README:
{{ rag_file('README.md')[0] }}

Research (cited):
{{ ref('1_b_research') | tojson }}

Return only JSON:
{
  "features": [
    {"id": "F1", "name": "...", "readme_row": "exact Item text from the scope table",
     "behaviour": "what the user sees", "acceptance": ["check runnable in CI, no printer"]}
  ],
  "ejectability_rules": [
    {"rule": "...", "threshold": "number + unit", "verdict_if_broken": "fail | warn", "source": "url or README"}
  ],
  "eject_block_params": [{"name": "...", "default": "concrete value", "ui_editable": true}],
  "api": [{"method": "POST", "path": "/...", "in": "...", "out": "..."}],
  "out_of_scope": ["..."],
  "open_questions": ["..."]
}
